    "live.staticflickr.com": "Direct Flickr image host serves any user. Classify per the Flickr user (whitehouse, number10gov, ukparliament \u2192 government). When a researcher cites a live.staticflickr.com URL, the image_candidate entry MUST include an explicit source_type field \u2014 the validator cannot infer it from the URL."
  },
  "thresholds": {
    "single_domain_max_pct": 50,
    "wikimedia_max_pct": 30,
    "wikimedia_max_count": 4,
    "min_distinct_source_types": 3,
    "min_unique_candidates": 16,
    "max_uses_per_url": 1,
    "_doc": "single_domain_max_pct is the RT-5 hard fail. wikimedia_max_pct and wikimedia_max_count are tighter editorial guidance (the lower of the two wins). min_distinct_source_types enforces the 3-of-5 menu. min_unique_candidates (v8.13.7) is the floor on distinct verified URLs the researcher must surface so writers can fill every chapter slot without reuse. max_uses_per_url (v8.13.7) is enforced by Phase 7.8 (visual-smoke-test.py D6) against the rendered DOM, not the bundle."
